      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: Krea 2 Anime-tuned Turbo",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Krea 2 Anime-tuned Turbo\n\nModel: [ricecake/Krea-2-Anime-tuned-Turbo](https://huggingface.co/ricecake/Krea-2-Anime-tuned-Turbo)\n\n## Model Links\n\n**diffusion_models**\n\n- [krea2_anime_tuned_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/ricecake/Krea-2-Anime-tuned-Turbo/resolve/main/krea2_anime_tuned_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors) (BF16 file and diffusers weights: see the model repo)\n\n**text_encoders** (Comfy-Org)\n\n- [qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors) (4.88 GB)\n\n**vae** (Comfy-Org)\n\n- [qwen_image_vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/resolve/main/vae/qwen_image_vae.safetensors) (242 MB)\n\nMore Krea 2 files: [Hugging Face:Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2), [ModelScope:Comfy-Org/Krea-2](https://modelscope.cn/models/Comfy-Org/Krea-2)\n\n## Model Storage Location\n\n```\nComfyUI/\n  models/\n    diffusion_models/\n      krea2_anime_tuned_turbo_fp8_scaled.safetensors\n    text_encoders/\n      qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors\n    vae/\n      qwen_image_vae.safetensors\n```\n\n## Caption node (capgen)\n\n**Krea 2 Anime Caption (capgen)** turns Danbooru tags into a caption in the style of the training captions; its `caption` output is the prompt. Install the custom node from [github.com/ricecake000/ComfyUI-Krea2-Anime-Capgen](https://github.com/ricecake000/ComfyUI-Krea2-Anime-Capgen) (it downloads its data, ~445 MB, on first use). The **info** preview shows how each tag was understood. To write your own prompt instead, delete the capgen node and type into the positive text box.\n\nAuto-generated captions often contain \"white background\" and lean towards Danbooru rating s (roughly R-12 to R-15 content). Remove what you do not want with exclusions in the tags, e.g. `-white background`, `-simple background`, or exclude suggestive tags.\n\n## Sampler settings\n\n8 steps, cfg 1.0 (no CFG; the negative is a zeroed copy of the positive, as in Comfy's Krea 2 Turbo template), euler / simple.\n\n**ModelSamplingFlux** with base_shift = max_shift = 1.15 gives Turbo's FIXED timestep shift mu = 1.15 at every resolution (the distilled checkpoint was trained at a fixed mu = 1.15). This is also ComfyUI's built-in Krea 2 default; the node only makes it explicit. Change the resolution only with the **Width** / **Height** nodes: they feed both the latent and ModelSamplingFlux. Do not edit the shift values by hand (the UI rounds edits to 0.01).\n"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
